      {
        "key": "b",
        "label": "(b)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 6,
          "ms": 12
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is common for wild rice plants to have grains with awns present.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Suggest a selective advantage to wild rice of having awns present on their grains.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 1,
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "17.2(1)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 1,
          "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>one</i></b><i> from: </i>",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "for seed dispersal <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "idea of protection <b>; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "anchor into the ground <b>; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "obtain more, nutrients / water <b>; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "er": [],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Selection changes populations through differences in reproductive success. The environment acts on existing variation; it does not produce a needed allele in response to need.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:17.2(1)",
                "ms:b#1"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Identify the inherited difference and selection pressure.",
            "Trace survival and reproduction to a change across generations."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
            {
              "text": "Saying that an individual develops a useful allele because it needs it",
              "basis": "inferred",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:17.2(1)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "type": "short"
      },
      {
        "key": "c",
        "label": "(c)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 6
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "One of the changes that occurred during the domestication of wild rice to cultivated rice was the loss of the awns from rice grains.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Farmers found that long awns made storing and processing rice grains more difficult.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It was also observed that rice plants that have grains with no awns have an increased grain yield.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "parts": [
          {
            "key": "c.i",
            "label": "(i)",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6,
              "ms": 12
            },
            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Explain the principles used by farmers to produce rice plant grains with no awns.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 6
                }
              }
            ],
            "marks": 4,
            "topics": [
              {
                "ref": "17.2(6)",
                "role": "primary"
              }
            ],
            "markScheme": {
              "marks": 4,
              "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>four</i></b><i> from: </i>",
              "guidance": [],
              "points": [
                {
                  "n": 1,
                  "text": "1  artificial selection / selective breeding / humans act as selection pressure <b>; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 2,
                  "text": "2  select (rice) plants / seeds / grains, with no awns <b>; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 3,
                  "text": "3  <i>idea of</i> breeding (selected) <u>plants</u><b> </b>/ self pollination of (selected) <u>plants</u> <b>;</b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 4,
                  "text": "4  seeds germinate / plants grow / offspring grow <b>;</b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 5,
                  "text": "5  repeat (selection and breeding) over generation<u>s</u> <b>;</b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 6,
                  "text": "6  AVP<b> ; </b>e.g. <i>ref. to</i> genetic technology<i> </i>detail of pollination",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                }
              ]
            },
            "er": [],
            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "Artificial selection depends on human choice of breeding individuals. Selection must be repeated across generations to increase the frequency of the desired inherited trait.",
                  "refs": [
                    "syllabus:17.2(6)",
                    "ms:c.i#1"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reasoningChain": [
                "Identify the desired phenotype and select parents.",
                "Describe breeding, selection of offspring and repetition."
              ],
              "inferredMistakes": [
                {
                  "text": "Confusing selective breeding with direct gene insertion",
                  "basis": "inferred",
                  "refs": [
                    "syllabus:17.2(6)"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "type": "short"
          },
          {
            "key": "c.ii",
            "label": "(ii)",
            "source": {
              "qp": 7,
              "ms": 13
            },
            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The normal allele for the gene <i>An‑1</i> codes for a transcription factor that has a role in awn development and in the number of grains of rice produced.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 7
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When the transcription factor is present there is:",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 7
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  "an increase in the expression of genes involved in awn development (positive regulation)",
                  "a decrease in the expression of genes involved in the number of grains produced (negative regulation)."
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Suggest <b>and</b> explain how changes at the <i>An‑1</i> locus can cause rice plants to have grains with no awns and an increased grain yield.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 7
                }
              }
            ],
            "marks": 3,
            "topics": [
              {
                "ref": "16.3(3)",
                "role": "primary"
              }
            ],
            "markScheme": {
              "marks": 3,
              "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>three</i></b><i> from: </i>",
              "guidance": [],
              "points": [
                {
                  "n": 1,
                  "text": "1  mutation / change in base sequence, (in <i>An-1</i>) <b>or </b> <b> </b> <i>An-1</i> <u>not</u> expressed <b>; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 2,
                  "text": "2  transcription factor has different, primary structure / tertiary structure / 3D shape <b> </b> <b>or </b> <b> </b> transcription factor <u>not</u>, produced / functional <b>or</b> transcription factor faulty <b>; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 3,
                  "text": "3  transcription factor does <u>not</u> bind to, the promoter / DNA <b>; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 4,
                  "text": "4  <u>decrease</u> in expression of gene(s) for awn development<b> ;</b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 5,
                  "text": "5  <u>increase</u> in expression of gene(s) for number of grains produced<b> ; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                }
              ]
            },
            "er": [],
            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "A transcription factor alters gene expression by binding particular DNA sequences. Changing the factor or its binding site can alter protein abundance without changing the target protein’s amino acid sequence.",
